            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="ROS05" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename/>
                        <surname>Rosser</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation>chemist?</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> The father of <persName key="ROS01">Henry Blanche Rosser</persName>, a Godwin 'pupil' who committed suicide in Paris in 1822. 
    There are then three entries for Rosser Sen'r - one within a week of Rosser's death, when Godwin calls on him;  and two subsequent occasions
    in August when Rosser calls on Godwin. 
    Rosser Senr is likely to be the partner in Warren and Roser (probably a chemist's), 5 Skinner Street,   who sold Epsom Salts
    (advertised <title>The Morning Chronicle</title>).
    The two entries in 1830 to C Rosser may be to another child of the family but these have been left uncoded.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="journalism"><title>The Morning Chronicle</title> , Wednesday, April 4, 1821.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
